  "description": "A research-informed introduction to autonomy and meaningful choices in roleplaying games, illustrated using Fallout 4 gameplay. Correlational findings from game motivation research are distinguished from game design interpretations.",
  "youtube_title": "Why RPG Choices Feel So Personal | Gaming Psychology",
  "social_caption": "Ever hesitated over a dialogue choice in an RPG? 🎮 Psychology offers one clue: autonomy — feeling that your decisions genuinely matter. We explore why three dialogue buttons don't always create meaningful choice. Based on Self-Determination Theory and studies of game enjoyment; this isn't a diagnosis of players. Which RPG made you stop and think? #Fallout4 #GamingPsychology #RPG #ThePlayerMind",
